<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n903" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">admixtĭo</span></b>  (better than <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">admist-</span></b> ),
		ōnis, f.
		admisceo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mingling;</i> in concreto, <i>an
				admixture</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animus omni admixtione corporis liberatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Sen. 22, 79</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terreni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 5, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ardor nulla admixtione concretus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 45, 117</span></i>
			.—In plur., <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 9, 2 al.</span></i></div>
